    {
      "id": "typed-inter-graph-handoff-envelope-instructions",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Proposed V1 Specification",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -220,
        "y": 700
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "typed-inter-graph-handoff-envelope"
        },
        "markdown": "## Use the graph as an argument\n\nKeep **Idea**, **Problem**, **Audience**, and **Proposed Approach** as singular anchors. Duplicate **Question**, **Assumption**, **Research**, **Evidence**, **Alternative**, **Risk**, and **Next Step** as the investigation grows.\n\nEvidence should support or contradict something specific. Next steps should test an assumption or question and name the evidence they are expected to produce.\n\nSee the adjacent `SKILL.md` before deriving a new graph.",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Proposed v1 handoff envelope\n\n```json\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"id\": \"handoff_01\",\n  \"correlationId\": \"run_01\",\n  \"mode\": \"send\",\n  \"lifetime\": \"ephemeral\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"graphRef\": \"github://.../host.node\",\n    \"graphId\": \"host\",\n    \"nodeId\": \"producer-script\",\n    \"portId\": \"result\"\n  },\n  \"destination\": {\n    \"graphRef\": \"github://.../fragment.node\",\n    \"graphId\": \"fragment\",\n    \"nodeId\": \"receiver\",\n    \"portId\": \"input\"\n  },\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"schema\": \"twilite://schema/text@1\",\n    \"contentType\": \"text/plain\",\n    \"value\": \"Hello from the host graph\"\n  },\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"runId\": \"run_01\",\n    \"producerType\": \"script\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-30T00:00:00.000Z\"\n  },\n  \"delivery\": {\n    \"attempt\": 1,\n    \"status\": \"proposed\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## V1 executable boundary\n\n- Support `mode: send` only.\n- Support `lifetime: ephemeral` only.\n- Require durable source and destination addresses down to the declared port.\n- Require a schema identifier and validate it against the destination input.\n- Require correlation and provenance fields.\n- Produce an inspectable `delivered` or `rejected` result.\n- Do not mutate the receiver when validation or delivery fails.\n- Do not make expansion a delivery side effect; the portal still owns expansion.\n\n## Reserved, not implemented in v1\n\n- `request-response` and `stream` modes\n- `session` and `durable` lifetimes\n- retries, replay, persistence, and fan-out\n\n## Review decisions\n\n1. Is `schema` the right identity, or should ports name a declaration-owned type contract?\n2. Is delivery status part of the envelope, or a separate immutable result linked by `id`?\n3. Does authorization belong in provenance, delivery context, or a separate runtime decision record?\n4. Which payload size forces a future stream instead of `send`?"
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        }
      },
