      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Make every cross-graph handoff an inspectable typed envelope",
        "statement": "When a graph sends data through an inter-graph edge, Twilite should deliver one explicit envelope containing the typed payload, both addressed endpoints, correlation and provenance, lifetime, delivery mode, and an observable outcome.",
        "status": "framed",
        "confidence": "promising",
        "notes": "The edge declares connectivity. The portal owns reversible expansion. The envelope carries data. The receiver consumes only through a declared input port.",
        "definitionKey": "idea",
        "_classBinding": {
