      "data": {
        "title": "Which parts belong in the first executable contract?",
        "question": "Should v1 execute only ephemeral send, or also session and durable lifetimes, request-response, and streams? How should schema identities and delivery acknowledgements be represented?",
        "status": "open",
        "answer": "Proposed review position: implement ephemeral send first; require addressed endpoints, schema/type, correlation, provenance, and explicit delivered or rejected results. Reserve other modes and lifetimes without pretending they work.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-question",
