        "title": "A complete-looking envelope could promise behavior we do not implement",
        "description": "Request-response, streams, durable delivery, retries, and replay each require lifecycle and authority decisions. Encoding them without enforcement would make the graph look safer and more capable than the runtime is.",
        "likelihood": "medium",
        "impact": "high",
        "mitigation": "Version the envelope, reject unsupported modes and lifetimes, ship ephemeral send first, expose every delivery result, and add capabilities only with canonical tests.",
